From cc4a3387269262be7e80c9624d52ebf36965fc77 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 07:14:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Distinguish demo from real manufacturer data

Reuse organizations.record_type (REAL/DEMO/TEST) as the classification.

- Eligibility: Visionary visibility and booking now require REAL data.
- Onboarding company lookup: REAL companies plus the viewer's own.
- Duplicate checks (CSV import, Admin Entry) keep DEMO records and report
  cross-type matches as conflicts, never converting them.
- CSV import requires --record-type; Admin Entry takes record_type.
- Changing the classification is limited to administrators/operators,
  requires a reason, and is recorded in change history.
- Admin list returns recordTypeCounts for All/Real/Demo tabs; the list
  shows a Real or Demo badge; the detail page has a confirmed control.
- Migration 023: re-assert record_type, add organizations.source_ref
  where missing, add record_type_classification_log.
- One-time scripts in database/backfills/023_demo_classification:
  preview, apply, verify, rollback.
- Docs: DEMO_REAL_DATA.md, README, API contract.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HzRHiDDMNJoYJD4rs7BHRX
